  "instructions": [
    "Heat butter in a large saucepan over medium heat.",
    "Add beef cutlet and cook until browned, about 3 minutes per side. Remove from heat and set aside.",
    "Add white wine to the saucepan and cook until reduced by half, about 2 minutes.",
    "Add chicken broth and bring to a boil.",
    "Add rice and cook, stirring constantly, until lightly toasted, about 2 minutes.",
    "Add lemon juice, orange zest, egg, kosher salt, and black pepper. Cook, stirring constantly, until the mixture is smooth and creamy, about 5 minutes.",
    "Cut the beef cutlet into thin strips and add to the saucepan. Cook for 1-2 minutes, until heated through.",
    "Stir in Gruyere cheese and cook until melted and bubbly, about 1 minute.",
    "Garnish with fresh parsley, fennel fronds, and serve immediately."
